Third-party code
----------------

The copyright notice above does not cover the following, which is the work of
others and is included with attribution:

shaders/phong.glsl
  The Phong lighting model (the Ka/Kd/Ks/shininessVal uniforms and the ambient,
  Lambertian diffuse and specular terms) is derived from the educational WebGL
  Phong applet by Prof. Thorsten Thormaehlen
  (https://multivis.net/lecture/phong.html), as modified by Johannes Kehrer and
  Alec Jacobson (https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~jacobson/phong-demo/). The upstream
  applet states no license; it is reproduced here with attribution only.

shaders/phong.glsl
  The rgb2hsv and hsv2rgb functions are by Sam Hocevar, from "Fast branchless
  RGB to HSV conversion in GLSL" (2013), originally published at
  http://lolengine.net/blog/2013/07/27/rgb-to-hsv-in-glsl and mirrored at
  https://gist.github.com/983/e170a24ae8eba2cd174f. The original post states no
  license; it is reproduced here with attribution only, as is conventional for
  this snippet.

example/
  The platform scaffolding under example/android, example/ios, example/linux,
  example/macos and example/windows is unmodified output of the `flutter create`
  templates, which are Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors and licensed under the
  BSD 3-Clause License (https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/master/LICENSE).
